# What EAS Build uploads. It archives the whole git root, which here is an
# ML monorepo — ~1.9 GB of tracked datasets and models that the Expo app in
# subproject/SDUI/kride has nothing to do with. Without this file the upload
# either takes forever or dies walking directories it never needed to read.
#
# Note this REPLACES .gitignore for EAS (eas-cli skips .gitignore entirely once
# .easignore exists), and unlike .gitignore it can also exclude tracked files —
# which is required here, since the large datasets are committed. node_modules
# is always ignored by eas-cli regardless.
#
# Allowlist: drop everything, then re-admit the path to the mobile workspace.
# Each level needs its contents excluded before the next can be re-included —
# a file cannot be re-included once a parent directory is excluded.
/*
!/subproject
/subproject/*
!/subproject/SDUI
/subproject/SDUI/*
!/subproject/SDUI/kride

# Local build outputs inside the workspace — regenerated on the build server.
**/.expo/
**/.next/
**/dist/
**/dist-*/
**/.eas-cli-tools/
**/.eas-npm-cache/
**/.eas-user-data/
**/node_modules.stale/
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.*
